target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestCheckReadsOmittedBranchesFromGit'
expect: did not make main the default
why:    `git symbolic-ref --short refs/remotes/origin/HEAD` answers "origin/main", not "main". Compared raw against the current branch it never matches, so the default-branch guard silently passes on the default branch itself — an auto-push to main with every other check green. The prefix is stripped, and an answer without it is treated as unknown.
--- old
	name, ok := strings.CutPrefix(out, "origin/")
	if !ok {
		return ""
	}
	return name
--- new
	return out
